window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"u": "index.html", "t": "Descote V2", "h": "Critical technology, Human chemistry", "d": "Valves for hazardous fluids: chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear. Pre-engineered or tailor-made, designed and built in Feyzin, France.", "x": "Critical technology, Human chemistry Fit for challenge We handle Hazardous Fluids for Critical, Severe, applications. Our mission is to tackle the most challenging fluids and process conditions, while driving Engineering towards optimized performance and sustainability. “When Quality shall exceed the Standards…” Discover Safety Reliability Sustainability Industries chemicals agrochemicals petrochemicals nuclear Fluids & applications Chlorine related Chlorine and its derivatives: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. → Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF): refrigerants, HF alkylation, semiconductors, the nuclear fuel cycle. → CN related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) and its derivatives: MMA and acrylic glass, amino acids. → Hydrogen related High-pressure hydrogen: valves defined project by project, up to Class 2500. → Other critical applications Hot oil, molten salt, ammonia and other severe services. → All fluids & applications The fluid families we handle, on one page. → Fit for purpose We offer customisable & taylor-made Solutions Technology designed for professionals who understand and value the need for experience, precision, and authentic craftsmanship. Pre-engineered or tailored to meet your specific needs, we assist you to define the best technical solution. “What deserve to be done, deserves to be done well” Nicolas Poussin Discover Engineering Development Reliability study Explore our solutions Our valve ranges Process / piping, instrumentation, storage, transport and fluid transfer: field-proven designs, adapted to your fluid. Process / Piping Instrumentation Storage Transport Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Engineering approach Materials Tightness Testing & traceability Authentic Driven Flexible Human Chemistry A unique engineering skillset dedicated to metalworking, binding mechanics and metallurgy, with applied fluid mechanics, fluid dynamics, and corrosion science. “What is essential is invisible to the eye” Antoine de Saint-Exupery Discover Global Solution for you, International presence Where to find us ? Our teams and partners are close to your plants — from Feyzin to the rest of the world. Our network"}, {"u": "after-sales.html", "t": "After sales, spare parts & repair shops | Descote V2", "h": "Trained hands and genuine parts for your descote valves", "d": "Genuine descote spare parts, approved repair shops trained by descote and local service to keep your valves fit for hazardous duty.", "x": "Home ▸ After sales Trained hands and genuine parts for your descote valves A descote valve is built for long service in hazardous duty. When it needs care, trained repairers and genuine parts keep it that way. Repair shops trained by descote Our approved repair shops are trained by descote and repair our valves close to your plant. Genuine descote spare parts Every descote valve has a unique serial number. Quote your valve's serial number: we identify the genuine parts that match it. Before you send a valve back For everyone's safety, a valve that has been in hazardous service must be decontaminated before it leaves your site and returned with a decontamination certificate. Contact us first: we will send you the form and the return instructions. Also at your service Expertise and repair Diagnosis and repair by our team in Feyzin. Instructions Installation, operation and maintenance instructions for each model. → Local stock Stock in Baton Rouge (USA); stock and after-sales service in Shanghai (China). → Your valve was defined for one service; its serial number lets us repair it to that same definition. Looking for a descote repair shop? Find the repair shops near your plant on our map, or send us an after-sales request. See the map After-sales request What next? References Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. References FAQ Short answers to the questions engineers and buyers ask us most often. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Solutions Process / Piping Storage Transport Instrumentation Fluids & applications All fluids & applications"}, {"u": "case-studies.html", "t": "Case studies: valves for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Case studies", "d": "Anonymised field results: descote valves in chlorine, HF, HCN, nuclear and other severe services. Filter by industry, valve type and area.", "x": "Home ▸ References ▸ Case studies Case studies Anonymised results from chlorine, hydrogen fluoride (HF), hydrogen cyanide (HCN), nuclear and other severe duties. Success stories Customer names withheld. Industry All Chemicals Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Fluid & application All Chlorine related Fluorine related CN related Other critical applications Type of valve All Manual On-off Control 3-way Check Area All North America Europe Asia Reset Actuated globe valves in descote yellow on an outdoor process line. Europe · Liquid and gaseous chlorine 400 valves for a new chlorine storage unit Manual, on-off, control and tank-bottom valves, 1\" to 10\", for storage, liquefaction and sampling. Process / Piping Storage Chlorine related Chemicals Valve nest on top of a vessel, reached through the service grating. Europe · Liquid chlorine Chlorine feed line: 20 years without maintenance A 1-inch 2100B on a liquid chlorine feed line, maintenance-free in 2022. Process / Piping Chlorine related Chemicals Motorized valve mounted directly beneath a large storage vessel. Asia · Liquid chlorine Liquid chlorine storage tanks 1½\" and 2\" bellows sealed globe valves on liquid chlorine storage tanks, at −4 °C and about 15 bar: no problem in four years. Storage Process / Piping Chlorine related Chemicals Valves inside the protective housing of a rail tank car, seen from above. North America · Liquid chlorine Chlorine tank cars across North America Over 1,000 double-closure 922/926 valves: bellows sealed angle valve plus internal check valve. Transport Chlorine related Chemicals Actuated bellows sealed globe valve on a process unit. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) HF alkylation in several refineries Isolation valves in HF alkylation units, praised for positive shut-off. Process / Piping Fluorine related Petrochemicals Large actuator on a valve assembly, with its control instrumentation. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) Bespoke actuator, HF alkylation safety system A 10-inch 2100HF valve replaced plug valves, with a fail-open actuator designed by descote. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Petrochemicals Top-mounted valves on a storage tank, painted descote yellow. North America · Anhydrous HF Anhydrous HF tank outlet Nickel-alloy bottom-outlet valves up to 8\": reliability study, helium testing, 18-metre manual extension. Storage Tailor-made Fluorine related Chemicals Valves around a process vessel, on a circular access platform. Europe · Fluorinated fluids (refrigerants) Refrigerants: in service since 1993 On corrosive, toxic fluorinated fluids, some valves ran without maintenance from 1993 to at least 2016. Process / Piping Fluorine related Chemicals Grey-painted piping and actuated valves on a skid in a process hall. Europe · Hydrogen fluoride (HF), gas mixtures Nuclear fuel: HF service since 1986 About 250 valves, including 3-way valves cycling every 12 minutes; no incident or HF leak reported by 2002. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Nuclear Actuated instrumentation valve among the stainless tubing of a laboratory installation. Europe · Heavy water, gases 950 valves for a nuclear research facility Manual, on-off, control and check valves up to 4\", fully documented in 1995; rated outstanding 20 years on. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Nuclear Bellows sealed globe valve next to a sampling station. North America · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) One valve, 14 shutdowns avoided An automated 2502 angle valve (1997) replaced a draw-off valve that failed at least twice a year; no failure by 2010. Process / Piping CN related Chemicals A row of manual globe valves with handwheels, ready for installation. Asia · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) 550+ valves for one HCN unit More than 550 manual and on-off 2500-series valves, 1\" to 6\", up to Class 1500, in a single HCN unit. Process / Piping CN related Chemicals Globe valve fitted with position instrumentation on a process line. Europe · Hot oil Hot-oil emergency shutdown valve An 8-inch on-off bellows sealed valve, helium-tested for fugitive emissions, designed for safety integrity level 2 (SIL 2). Process / Piping Other critical applications Petrochemicals Jacketed globe valve on its shipping crate: the outer jacket carries the heating medium. Asia · Molten salt 69 jacketed valves for molten salt 2500J bellows sealed valves with heat-jacketed body and bonnet keep molten salt at +400 °C. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals Pipe racks and valves of a process plant. Europe · Hydrogen Hydrogen at 420 bar A 1-inch Class 2500 gland packed valve for 420 bar, replacing a 2002 descote valve. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals No case study matches these filters. Each valve was specified for its own fluid, conditions and plant. The same checks now apply to every duty: each bellows helium-tested, each valve pressure-tested and serial-numbered. Discuss your requirements Facing a similar duty? Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. References Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. Solutions All solutions Process / Piping Transport Storage Tailor-made Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related CN related Other critical applications Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "company.html", "t": "About us: valves for hazardous fluids since 1974 | Descote V2", "h": "Valve specialists for hazardous fluids since 1974", "d": "descote designs, manufactures and tests valves for hazardous fluids in Feyzin, France. Our history, values, key figures and international presence.", "x": "Home ▸ Company Valve specialists for hazardous fluids since 1974 descote designs, manufactures and tests valves for hazardous fluids, from toxic and corrosive chemicals to liquefied gases, in a single factory in Feyzin, France. About descote Today descote serves the chemical, agrochemical, petrochemical and nuclear industries worldwide. Our core technology is the bellows sealed globe valve: a metal bellows seals the moving stem, with a packing as back-up. We also make gland packed valves, check valves, storage, transport and instrumentation valves, and fluid transfer ejectors. Our engineers work from your fluid, your process conditions and your specification, and the valve design follows from them. Feyzin factory tour History 1974 Under new ownership, descote specialises in globe valves for hazardous fluids. 1979 The US Department of Energy accepts our valves for uranium hexafluoride (UF6) cylinders. 1983 First approval of our globe valves for liquid chlorine, by the BITC (Bureau International Technique du Chlore), which became Euro Chlor in 1989. 1989 First ISO approval of our quality system. 2009 descote leaves the Tyco group after ten years. Its 1974 owner, his son and an American partner buy it back, and it takes back its name. 2014 Our main globe valve series are certified SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) by exida, to IEC 61508. 2020 descote Inc. opens in Baton Rouge, USA. 2021 Euro Chlor approval (GEST 17/492) of models 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC; fugitive emission qualification (leaks to the air) to EN ISO 15848-1 for selected models. 2025 Our service centre for Asia-Pacific opens in Shanghai. Values and commitments Safety Our valves contain fluids that can harm people, plants and the environment. Protecting lives comes first. Reliability A globe valve closes by pressing, not sliding, which avoids friction and jamming over time. Sustainability Bellows stem seals, backed up by packing, help keep hazardous fluids from escaping along the stem into the air. Key figures 50+ years designing valves for hazardous fluids 1 factory in Feyzin: design, manufacturing and testing under one roof 60+ countries on our global presence map Quality & certification Every bellows is helium-tested and every valve pressure-tested. Each valve leaves Feyzin with its own serial number and manufacturer's certificate, under our ISO 9001:2015 quality system, first approved in 1989. See our certificates → International presence Feyzin, France Headquarters, engineering and manufacturing. Baton Rouge, USA descote Inc.: local stock of valves and actuators. Shanghai, China descote Valve (Shanghai) Co., Ltd.: stock, customisation and after-sales for Asia-Pacific. Worldwide Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. → Critical Technology, Human Chemistry: our engineers define each valve with you, then our workshop builds, tests and traces it in Feyzin. Discuss your requirements Tell us about your fluid and conditions: our engineers will answer. Send an inquiry What next? descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. descote Globally Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Solutions Tailor-made All solutions Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related CN related Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "cookies.html", "t": "Cookie Policy | Descote V2", "h": "Cookie Policy", "d": "Which cookies the descote website uses, what they do, how long they last and how to change your choice at any time.", "x": "Home ▸ Cookie Policy Cookie Policy Which cookies this website uses, why, and how to change your choice. What is a cookie? A cookie is a small text file stored on your device when you visit a website. It lets the site recognise your device and remember information about your visit. Cookies we use We measure audience with Matomo, hosted on our own website. _pk_id.* Audience measurement: stores a unique visit identifier. Lifetime: 13 months. _pk_ref.* Audience measurement: records how you arrived on the site. Lifetime: 6 months. _pk_ses.* Audience measurement: stores your visit data temporarily. Lifetime: 30 minutes. hasConsent Remembers your cookie choice so the banner is not shown again. Lifetime: 7 months. External services Some features rely on external providers, which may set their own cookies or collect technical data such as your IP address. Form protection Anti-spam check on our forms (currently Google reCAPTCHA). Your choices You can accept or refuse non-essential cookies in the cookie banner, and change your choice at any time with the Cookie settings link at the bottom of each page. You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings; some features may then no longer work. How long we keep data Cookies and browsing data are kept for 13 months at most. To find out how we handle personal data, please read our Privacy Policy. The traceability we apply to every valve applies here too: each cookie is listed with its purpose and lifetime. A question about cookies? Write to info@descote.com. Privacy Policy How descote handles your personal data. What next? Legal information Privacy Policy Legal information Legal notices Legal information Terms and Conditions The terms that apply when you use the descote website."}, {"u": "faq.html", "t": "FAQ: bellows sealed valves for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Frequently asked questions", "d": "Answers on descote bellows sealed globe valves: technology, selection, Euro Chlor, SIL, fugitive emissions, testing, spare parts and repairs.", "x": "Home ▸ References ▸ FAQ Frequently asked questions What engineers and buyers ask us most. All Technology Selection Certifications Quality Service Why a bellows sealed globe valve for hazardous fluids? The stem, the usual leak path, is sealed by a welded multi-ply metal bellows, backed up by a packing. 2100 or 2500 series: what is the difference? The 2100 bellows sits inside the bonnet, protected from the flow. The 2500 bellows is swept by the flow, suiting fluids that polymerise or crystallise. Can a globe valve replace a gate, plug or ball valve? It can, at the same face-to-face (installed length). Globe valves pass less flow than full-bore valves, so we check your flow coefficient (Cv) first. Which fluids do you handle? Hazardous fluids where a small leak can cause serious harm (ASME B31.3 Category M): chlorine, hydrogen chloride, hydrogen fluoride (HF), hydrogen cyanide, phosgene. What do you need to prepare a quotation? Fluid, water content, design pressure and temperatures, size, class, end connections, actuation, applicable standards and country of installation. Can you build to our own specification? Yes, including your country's codes; any deviation is agreed before manufacture. Earlier on, we can help with sizing and material selection. Do your chlorine valves meet Euro Chlor recommendations? Models 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC are Euro Chlor approved (GEST 17/492), within defined sizes and classes. Approval certificates on request. Are your valves rated for safety integrity level (SIL)? Several series and our BIMATIC actuators are certified SIL 3 capable by exida (IEC 61508); your function's SIL is calculated on the whole loop. Do your valves meet fugitive emission standards? Selected manual and on-off models are type-tested to EN ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and German TA Luft rules, within stated limits; control valves excluded. Do you supply valves for HF alkylation units? Yes. Licensor Honeywell UOP has accepted our designs; manual and on-off models are declared compliant with MSS SP-160 and API RP 751. How is each valve tested? Alloys are checked on receipt, machined and welded parts dye-penetrant tested, every bellows helium-tested, every valve shell- and seat-tested. What documents come with each valve? A manufacturer's certificate tied to the valve's unique serial number, with EN 10204 3.1 material certificates and test results. How do I order spare parts? Quote your valve's serial number: we identify the genuine parts that match it. Can I return a valve for repair? Yes, decontaminated and with a signed decontamination certificate. Contact us first: an approved repair shop nearby may help. Most answers depend on your duty: we define each valve around it, then test it before shipment. Still have a question? Our engineers will answer. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. References Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. descote After sales Spare parts and approved repair shops. Solutions Process / Piping All solutions Tailor-made Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related CN related"}, {"u": "fluid-chlorine.html", "t": "Valves for chlorine, HCl and phosgene | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for the chlorine chain", "d": "Bellows sealed globe valves for chlorine, anhydrous HCl and phosgene. Chlorine valves Euro Chlor approved (GEST 17/492).", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications ▸ Chlorine related Valves for the chlorine chain Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene are toxic, corrosive and react with moisture. From electrolysis to tank car loading, descote valves keep them contained. Application families Chloromethanes Solvents and chemical intermediates. PVC Vinyl chloride and PVC. Isocyanates Isocyanates for polyurethanes. Polysilicon A base material of the semiconductor industry. Synthetic rubbers Chlorine-based synthetic rubbers. What chlorine demands Liquid chlorine and dry chlorine gas Moisture makes chlorine corrosive: every valve is degreased and dried for halogen service; every bellows is helium-tested. Anhydrous HCl It cools sharply as it expands, so materials are chosen for the lowest temperature. Phosgene Extremely toxic. Double-containment designs are available on request. Solutions for this fluid ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves, including double containment. 2100B 2100BAT 2100BAC Explore the range → Storage Top and bottom tank valves, remotely operated. 2200 2300 Explore the range → Transport Tank car valves approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). 921 925/926 Explore the range → Each chlorine valve is defined for its line and standard, then traced from raw material to final test. Valves to Euro Chlor GEST 17/492 Our 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC valves, 1\" to 6\", are Euro Chlor approved to GEST 17/492, the European specification for chlorine valves. Certificates on request. Our first liquid-chlorine valves were approved in 1983. SIL 3 capable (IEC 61508) Safety integrity level (SIL) 3 capable: 2100 and 2200/2300 valves, BIMATIC actuators. Proven in the field Valves inside the protective housing of a rail tank car, seen from above. North America · Liquid chlorine Chlorine tank cars across North America Over 1,000 double-closure 922/926 valves: bellows sealed angle valve plus internal check valve. Transport Chlorine related Chemicals Actuated globe valves in descote yellow on an outdoor process line. Europe · Liquid and gaseous chlorine 400 valves for a new chlorine storage unit Manual, on-off, control and tank-bottom valves, 1\" to 10\", for storage, liquefaction and sampling. Process / Piping Storage Chlorine related Chemicals Valve nest on top of a vessel, reached through the service grating. Europe · Liquid chlorine Chlorine feed line: 20 years without maintenance A 1-inch 2100B on a liquid chlorine feed line, maintenance-free in 2022. Process / Piping Chlorine related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Request On-off actuated bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAT Request Control bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAC Request All literature → FAQ Why a bellows sealed globe valve for dry chlorine? The disc lifts straight off the seat without sliding friction, so deposits do not jam it; a welded metal bellows seals the stem. Do you supply valves for wet chlorine? Wet chlorine needs different materials: send us your conditions for review. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Other fluids & applications Fluorine related CN related Other critical applications Discuss your requirements Share your fluid, operating conditions and standards: we will define the valve for your line. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Solution Storage Top and bottom tank valves with an internal safety check valve and remote closure. descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations."}, {"u": "fluid-cn.html", "t": "Valves for hydrogen cyanide (HCN) service | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for hydrogen cyanide chemistry", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for hydrogen cyanide (HCN) service: MMA and acrylic glass, amino acids, acrylic rubber.", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications ▸ CN related Valves for hydrogen cyanide chemistry Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) is a building block for methyl methacrylate (MMA), acrylic glass and amino acids. It is extremely toxic, flammable and can polymerise inside the line. Application families MMA and acrylic glass Methyl methacrylate (MMA) and its polymer, acrylic glass (PMMA). Amino acids Amino acids for animal feed. Acrylic rubber Specialty synthetic rubber. What HCN demands Polymerisation Stagnant HCN can polymerise in packings and cavities and seize the stem. In our 2500 series, the bellows sits in the flow, which keeps it flushed. Toxicity A welded metal bellows, backed by a secondary packing, contains the fluid at the stem. Solidification Products that solidify as they cool need heated jacketed valves, which keep them above their solidification point. Solutions for this fluid ← → Process / Piping Exposed-bellows and gland packed globe valves, straight or angle. 2500B 2500BAT 2502 1500B Explore the range → Storage Isolation valves for HCN storage tanks. Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Heated jacketed valves. Explore the range → For HCN, the design follows the process: bellows position, heating and materials are chosen service by service. Proven in the field A row of manual globe valves with handwheels, ready for installation. Asia · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) 550+ valves for one HCN unit More than 550 manual and on-off 2500-series valves, 1\" to 6\", up to Class 1500, in a single HCN unit. Process / Piping CN related Chemicals Bellows sealed globe valve next to a sampling station. North America · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) One valve, 14 shutdowns avoided An automated 2502 angle valve (1997) replaced a draw-off valve that failed at least twice a year; no failure by 2010. Process / Piping CN related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Request Gland packed globe valve, Model 1500B Request All literature → FAQ Model 2500 or 2100 for HCN? It depends on the process. Our 2500, with its bellows in the flow, is recommended where polymerisation is a risk; our engineers confirm the choice for each service. Can valves be heated? Yes. Jacketed versions keep body and bonnet at process temperature. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Other fluids & applications Chlorine related Other critical applications Discuss your requirements Tell us your fluid, its stabilisation, temperature and pressure. We will define the valve with you. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed and gland packed globe valves, 3-way and check valves for process lines. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. References Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia."}, {"u": "fluid-fluorine.html", "t": "Valves for HF alkylation and fluorine chemistry | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for fluorine chemistry", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for anhydrous HF and fluorine chemistry: refrigerants, HF alkylation, BF3, semiconductors and the nuclear fuel cycle.", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications ▸ Fluorine related Valves for fluorine chemistry Anhydrous hydrogen fluoride (AHF) is the backbone of fluorine chemistry. It is highly toxic, causes deep burns and boils at 19.5 °C: every joint and seal counts. Application families Refrigerants Hydrofluorocarbon (HFC) and hydrofluoroolefin (HFO) refrigerants. HF alkylation Refinery units where hydrogen fluoride is the catalyst for cleaner fuels. BF3 Boron trifluoride, a polymerisation catalyst. Semiconductors Fluorinated electronic gases used to make chips and displays. Nuclear fuel cycle Uranium conversion and enrichment. → What HF demands Toxicity Highly toxic: a welded metal bellows, backed by packing, seals the stem, the usual leak path. Deep burns HF causes deep burns on contact: every joint and seal counts. Low boiling point Anhydrous HF boils at 19.5 °C: every bellows is helium-tested for tightness. HF alkylation: accepted designs The process licensor Honeywell UOP has accepted our globe and gate valve designs for its HF piping classes. Our manual and on-off valves are declared compliant with MSS SP-160, the HF alkylation valve standard, and API RP 751, the recommended practice for these units. Nuclear: fluorine at the heart of the fuel cycle Uranium conversion and enrichment rely on hydrogen fluoride, fluorine and uranium hexafluoride (UF6). See our nuclear page. Nuclear → Solutions for this fluid ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe and gate valves, gland packed valves, lift check valves. 2100HF series 8000HF check valve Explore the range → Storage Primary isolation valves for AHF tanks. Explore the range → Transport AHF version of our tank car valves. 925/926 Explore the range → In HF service, trims, actuators and extensions are engineered for each unit, not picked from a catalogue. Proven in the field Actuated bellows sealed globe valve on a process unit. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) HF alkylation in several refineries Isolation valves in HF alkylation units, praised for positive shut-off. Process / Piping Fluorine related Petrochemicals Top-mounted valves on a storage tank, painted descote yellow. North America · Anhydrous HF Anhydrous HF tank outlet Nickel-alloy bottom-outlet valves up to 8\": reliability study, helium testing, 18-metre manual extension. Storage Tailor-made Fluorine related Chemicals Valves around a process vessel, on a circular access platform. Europe · Fluorinated fluids (refrigerants) Refrigerants: in service since 1993 On corrosive, toxic fluorinated fluids, some valves ran without maintenance from 1993 to at least 2016. Process / Piping Fluorine related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature HF alkylation: process valves Request HF alkylation: small-size valves Request All literature → FAQ Can a globe valve replace the plug valves of an HF alkylation unit? It can: versions with the same face-to-face dimensions fit existing piping. A globe valve has a lower flow coefficient (Cv), so we check the required flow with you first. Do you handle fluorine gas (F2)? Fluorine is the strongest known oxidiser: we review each request case by case. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Petrochemicals Refineries, with HF alkylation units first. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Other fluids & applications Chlorine related Other critical applications Discuss your requirements Send us your unit, fluid and piping class. We will propose the right valve and trim. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed and gland packed globe valves, 3-way and check valves for process lines. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Industry Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities."}, {"u": "fluid-other.html", "t": "Valves for other critical applications | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for other critical applications", "d": "Valves for high-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services, defined for each fluid.", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications ▸ Other critical applications Valves for other critical applications Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry are our core business, but the same engineering serves other severe duties: high-pressure hydrogen, toxic gases, very high temperatures. Application families Hydrogen High-pressure hydrogen: valves up to Class 2500, defined project by project. Ammonia and hydrogen sulphide Toxic liquefied gases, among the fluids of our 2200/2300 tank valves. Hot oil Isolation and emergency shutdown on hot, flammable heat-transfer oils. Molten salt Heated jacketed valves stop the salt from freezing in the line. What severe services demand Temperature From very low to very high temperatures: body, bellows and seat materials are selected for each service. Pressure Dedicated high-pressure series, bellows sealed or gland packed. Functional safety Our 1500, 2100, 2500 and 2200/2300 valve series and BIMATIC actuators are safety integrity level (SIL) 3 capable to IEC 61508. We supply the certification data; the SIL achieved depends on the complete loop. Solutions for this fluid ← → Process / Piping Manual, on-off and control valves, including high-pressure series. 2100BAT 2500 Explore the range → Storage Top and bottom tank valves for liquefied gases. 2200 2300 Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Heated jacketed valves, special materials and tests. Explore the range → Outside our core fields, the method stays the same: the valve is defined from your fluid data, then shell- and seat-tested before delivery. Proven in the field Pipe racks and valves of a process plant. Europe · Hydrogen Hydrogen at 420 bar A 1-inch Class 2500 gland packed valve for 420 bar, replacing a 2002 descote valve. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals Globe valve fitted with position instrumentation on a process line. Europe · Hot oil Hot-oil emergency shutdown valve An 8-inch on-off bellows sealed valve, helium-tested for fugitive emissions, designed for safety integrity level 2 (SIL 2). Process / Piping Other critical applications Petrochemicals Jacketed globe valve on its shipping crate: the outer jacket carries the heating medium. Asia · Molten salt 69 jacketed valves for molten salt 2500J bellows sealed valves with heat-jacketed body and bonnet keep molten salt at +400 °C. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Request Gland packed globe valve, Model 1500B Request BIMATIC linear pneumatic actuator Request All literature → FAQ Is my fluid within your scope? If it is toxic, corrosive, flammable, very hot or under high pressure, it may well be. Send us its safety data sheet and your operating conditions. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Petrochemicals Refineries, with HF alkylation units first. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Other fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related CN related Discuss your requirements A severe service outside our usual fields? Describe it: our engineers will tell you what we can do. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. Industry Petrochemicals Refineries, with HF alkylation units first."}, {"u": "fluids.html", "t": "Fluids & applications: valves for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Hazardous fluids we handle", "d": "Chlorine, fluorine, hydrogen cyanide, hydrogen and other critical fluids: descote valves are defined for each fluid, process and standard.", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications Hazardous fluids we handle descote works where a leak is not an option. Choose your fluid to see its main applications, what it demands and our solutions for it. Our fluid families Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. → Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases: refrigerants, HF alkylation, semiconductors, nuclear. → CN related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN): MMA and acrylic glass, amino acids, acrylic rubber. → Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services. → One method, whatever the fluid The fluids change; the method does not. Our engineers define each valve for its fluid, its operating conditions and your site standards. It is then made in Feyzin, France, tested and fully traceable. Prefer to start from your sector? Chemicals, agrochemicals, petrochemicals or nuclear: start from your sector to find the fluids and solutions that concern it. Industries → Four fluid families, one rule: the valve is engineered for the service, never the other way round. Discuss your requirements Tell us your fluid and operating conditions. Our engineers will point you to the right solution. Send an inquiry What next? Overview Industries Chemicals, agrochemicals, petrochemicals and nuclear. Overview Solutions Pre-engineered and tailor-made valves for process piping, instrumentation, storage and transport, plus jet ejectors for fluid transfer. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers."}, {"u": "industries.html", "t": "Industries we serve | Descote V2", "h": "Industries we serve", "d": "descote serves the chemical, agrochemical, petrochemical and nuclear industries. Choose your sector, or start from your fluid.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries Industries we serve descote serves the chemical, agrochemical, petrochemical and nuclear industries worldwide. Choose your sector to see the families we work for and the solutions that fit. Four sectors Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. → Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. → Petrochemicals Refineries, with HF alkylation units first. → Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. → Prefer to start from your fluid? Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids: start from your fluid in Fluids & applications. Both lead to the same product families. Fluids & applications → Four sectors, one rule: the valve is engineered for the service, never the other way round. Discuss your requirements Tell us your fluid and operating conditions. Our engineers will point you to the right solution. Send an inquiry What next? Overview Fluids & applications Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids. Overview Solutions Pre-engineered and tailor-made valves for process piping, instrumentation, storage and transport, plus jet ejectors for fluid transfer. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers."}, {"u": "industry-agrochemicals.html", "t": "Valves for the agrochemical industry | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for the agrochemical industry", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for crop protection plants: herbicides, insecticides, fungicides. Chlorine chemistry and other toxic fluids kept contained.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries ▸ Agrochemicals Valves for the agrochemical industry Making crop protection products can involve hazardous fluids such as chlorine and its derivatives. descote valves keep them contained. descote in agrochemicals We serve producers of crop protection products, or pesticides. Their plants can handle the same hazardous fluids as the chemical industry, such as chlorine and its derivatives or hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Families we serve Herbicides Crop protection against weeds. Insecticides Crop protection against insects. Fungicides Crop protection against fungal diseases. Solutions for this industry ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves, manual, on-off and control, for toxic and corrosive process fluids. Explore the range → Storage Top and bottom tank valves for liquefied toxic gases such as chlorine, with remote closure. Explore the range → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for gauges, transmitters and sampling points. Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Valves defined from your fluid data when no existing design fits. Explore the range → Whatever the active ingredient, the valve is defined from your fluid data, then shell- and seat-tested before delivery. Proven in the field Agrochemical case studies are in preparation. Tell us about your application. Share your application All case studies → Fluids & applications Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. CN related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Other industries Chemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Discuss your requirements Tell us your fluid and operating conditions. Our engineers will define the valve with you. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed and gland packed globe valves, 3-way and check valves for process lines. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Fluid & application Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more."}, {"u": "industry-chemicals.html", "t": "Valves for the chemical industry | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for the chemical industry", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry: PVC, isocyanates, refrigerants, acrylics. Made in Feyzin, France.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries ▸ Chemicals Valves for the chemical industry Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry are our core business. descote valves keep their toxic and corrosive fluids contained. descote in chemicals In chemical plants, our valves handle chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl), phosgene, hydrogen fluoride (HF) and hydrogen cyanide (HCN), from storage tanks and tank cars to process lines. Each valve is defined for its fluid and its line. Families we serve PVC Chlorine and hydrogen chloride lines along the PVC chain. Isocyanates Chlorine and phosgene service for the building blocks of polyurethanes. Other chlorine chemistry Chloromethanes, polysilicon, synthetic rubbers. Fluorochemicals Refrigerants, built on anhydrous hydrogen fluoride. Acrylics Methyl methacrylate (MMA) and acrylic glass, on the hydrogen cyanide route. Solutions for this industry ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves, manual, on-off and control, with Euro Chlor approved models for chlorine. Explore the range → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for gauges, transmitters and sampling points. Explore the range → Storage Top and bottom tank valves for liquefied toxic gases, with remote closure. Explore the range → Transport Tank car valves approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Valves defined with you when no existing design fits, such as heated jacketed valves. Explore the range → Each valve is defined for its fluid and its line, then made in Feyzin, France, tested and fully traceable. Proven in the field Valves inside the protective housing of a rail tank car, seen from above. North America · Liquid chlorine Chlorine tank cars across North America Over 1,000 double-closure 922/926 valves: bellows sealed angle valve plus internal check valve. Transport Chlorine related Chemicals Valves around a process vessel, on a circular access platform. Europe · Fluorinated fluids (refrigerants) Refrigerants: in service since 1993 On corrosive, toxic fluorinated fluids, some valves ran without maintenance from 1993 to at least 2016. Process / Piping Fluorine related Chemicals Bellows sealed globe valve next to a sampling station. North America · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) One valve, 14 shutdowns avoided An automated 2502 angle valve (1997) replaced a draw-off valve that failed at least twice a year; no failure by 2010. Process / Piping CN related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature General brochure: manufacturing programme Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Request All literature → Fluids & applications Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. CN related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services. Other industries Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Discuss your requirements Tell us your product, your fluid and your operating conditions. Our engineers will define the valve with you. Send an inquiry What next? Fluid & application Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations."}, {"u": "industry-nuclear.html", "t": "Valves and ejectors for the nuclear fuel cycle | Descote V2", "h": "Valves and ejectors for the nuclear fuel cycle", "d": "Bellows sealed valves and steam jet ejectors for conversion, enrichment, fuel fabrication, reprocessing and research facilities.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries ▸ Nuclear Valves and ejectors for the nuclear fuel cycle Nuclear facilities handle fluids that are both chemically aggressive and radioactive. descote has worked for the nuclear industry since 1974. descote in the nuclear industry We supply valves and steam jet ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion and enrichment to fuel fabrication and reprocessing, and to research facilities. Where the fluid is radioactive, our ejectors move it with no moving parts. Across the fuel cycle Conversion Bellows sealed valves for anhydrous hydrogen fluoride (HF) and uranium hexafluoride (UF6) lines. Enrichment Valves for UF6 process lines. Fuel fabrication HF lines in the conversion of UF6 to uranium oxide. UF6 transport Cylinder valves to ANSI N14.1. Reprocessing and MOX Steam jet ejectors transfer radioactive liquids in reprocessing and mixed-oxide (MOX) fuel plants. Research facilities Valves for heavy water (D2O) circuits; ejectors for research centres. What the fuel cycle demands Chemistry and radioactivity UF6 reacts with moisture to form HF. Tightness to the atmosphere comes first. Frequent cycling Some on-off valves operate very often: bellows life must be designed and proven. Nuclear quality Complete documentation and traceability for every valve. Solutions for this industry ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves, manual and on-off, for HF and UF6 lines. Explore the range → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for measuring and sampling points. Explore the range → Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Steam jet ejectors, characterised on our own test bench in Feyzin. Explore the range → Transport The 1-inch valve for UF6 cylinders. UF6 valve – Model 1000 Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Equipment engineered for its step of the fuel cycle. Explore the range → From high-cycling on-off valves to steam jet ejectors, each piece of equipment is engineered for its step of the fuel cycle. Proven in the field Grey-painted piping and actuated valves on a skid in a process hall. Europe · Hydrogen fluoride (HF), gas mixtures Nuclear fuel: HF service since 1986 About 250 valves, including 3-way valves cycling every 12 minutes; no incident or HF leak reported by 2002. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Nuclear Actuated instrumentation valve among the stainless tubing of a laboratory installation. Europe · Heavy water, gases 950 valves for a nuclear research facility Manual, on-off, control and check valves up to 4\", fully documented in 1995; rated outstanding 20 years on. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Nuclear All case studies → Related literature Valves for the nuclear industry Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Request All literature → FAQ How do you handle nuclear quality requirements? Our nuclear quality assurance follows ASME NQA-1 and 10 CFR 50 Appendix B. Send your requirements with your inquiry: documentation and traceability are agreed with you for each project. All questions → Fluids & applications Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services. Other industries Chemicals Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Discuss your requirements Describe your step of the fuel cycle, your fluid and your quality requirements. Our engineers will answer. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Ejectors driven by steam move radioactive and hazardous fluids, with no pump and no moving parts. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations."}, {"u": "industry-petrochemicals.html", "t": "Valves for refineries and HF alkylation | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for refineries and HF alkylation", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for refineries and HF alkylation units, accepted by licensor Honeywell UOP for its HF piping classes.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries ▸ Petrochemicals Valves for refineries and HF alkylation In refineries, descote valves contain anhydrous hydrogen fluoride (HF) in HF alkylation units, and serve other severe duties. HF alkylation Anhydrous HF is the catalyst that makes alkylate for cleaner fuels. The process licensor Honeywell UOP has accepted our globe and gate valve designs for its HF piping classes. Our manual and on-off valves are declared compliant with MSS SP-160, the HF alkylation valve standard, and API RP 751, the recommended practice for these units. Families we serve HF alkylation units Isolation and on-off valves for HF service, accepted by the licensor Honeywell UOP. Refineries Other severe refinery services. Solutions for this industry ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe and gate valves, gland packed valves and lift check valves for HF service. Explore the range → Storage Primary isolation valves for anhydrous HF tanks. Explore the range → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for HF service. Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Trims, actuators and extensions engineered for each unit. Explore the range → Every bellows is helium-tested and every valve pressure-tested before it leaves Feyzin, France. Proven in the field Actuated bellows sealed globe valve on a process unit. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) HF alkylation in several refineries Isolation valves in HF alkylation units, praised for positive shut-off. Process / Piping Fluorine related Petrochemicals Large actuator on a valve assembly, with its control instrumentation. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) Bespoke actuator, HF alkylation safety system A 10-inch 2100HF valve replaced plug valves, with a fail-open actuator designed by descote. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Petrochemicals Globe valve fitted with position instrumentation on a process line. Europe · Hot oil Hot-oil emergency shutdown valve An 8-inch on-off bellows sealed valve, helium-tested for fugitive emissions, designed for safety integrity level 2 (SIL 2). Process / Piping Other critical applications Petrochemicals All case studies → Related literature HF alkylation: process valves Request HF alkylation: small-size valves Request All literature → FAQ Can a globe valve replace the plug valves of an HF alkylation unit? It can: versions with the same face-to-face dimensions fit existing piping. A globe valve has a lower flow coefficient (Cv), so we check the required flow with you first. All questions → Fluids & applications Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services. Other industries Chemicals Agrochemicals Nuclear Discuss your requirements Send us your unit, fluid and piping class. We will propose the right valve and trim. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed and gland packed globe valves, 3-way and check valves for process lines. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Fluid & application Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases: refrigerants, HF alkylation, semiconductors, nuclear."}, {"u": "literature.html", "t": "Literature: brochures & manuals | Descote V2", "h": "Literature", "d": "Technical brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions for descote bellows sealed valves and actuators, available on request.", "x": "Home ▸ References ▸ Literature Literature Brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions for our valves and actuators, sent on request. Documents Type All Technical brochure Maintenance manual Safety instructions Category All Process / Piping Instrumentation Transport Storage All ranges Reset General brochure: manufacturing programme Technical brochure · All ranges Request Gland packed globe valve, Model 1500B Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request On-off actuated bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAT Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Control bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAC Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request 3-way valves, Models 3100 & 3500 Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Lift check valve, Model 8000 Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request BIMATIC linear pneumatic actuator Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request HF alkylation: process valves Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request HF alkylation: small-size valves Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Instrumentation bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2020 Technical brochure · Instrumentation Request Storage tank valves, Models 2200 & 2300 Technical brochure · Storage Request Trailer & rail transportation valves Technical brochure · Transport Request 1-inch valve for UF6 cylinders Technical brochure · Transport Request Valves for the nuclear industry Technical brochure · All ranges Request Models 1500B & 1500BAT Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Models 2100B, 2100BAT & 3-way valves Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Models 2500 & 2500AT Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Models 2100HF, 2100HFAT & 2100HFAC Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Model 8000 lift check valve Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Model 2020 instrumentation valve Maintenance manual · Instrumentation Request Models 2200 & 2300 storage valves Maintenance manual · Storage Request Models 921, 925 & 926 tank car valves Maintenance manual · Transport Request BIMATIC actuator Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Operating & safety instructions, all models Safety instructions · All ranges Request No document matches these filters. Every document here describes a starting point; your valve is then defined around your specification. Your valve, your documents Brochures show our base designs. The valve you order is engineered for your duty and ships with its own test records and material certificates. Request documents Full name * Company * Business email * Country * Industry Select… Chemicals Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Other Documents and languages * I agree to the Privacy Policy . * Send my request Mock-up: nothing is sent. * required Thank you — your request has been noted. The descote team will get back to you shortly. Didn't find what you were looking for? Contact us What next? descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. References FAQ Short answers to the questions engineers and buyers ask us most often. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Solutions Process / Piping Instrumentation Transport Storage All solutions Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "quality-certification.html", "t": "Quality & certification: tests and approvals | Descote V2", "h": "Quality you can trace, certificates you can check", "d": "ISO 9001 quality management, in-house testing and full traceability. Browse descote certificates and approvals: free download or on request.", "x": "Home ▸ Quality & Certification Quality you can trace, certificates you can check Our certificates, approvals and declarations, and the quality system behind every valve, from raw material to shipment. Our approach to quality Our quality management system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 by LRQA, with a first ISO approval in 1989. It covers design, manufacturing, sales and customer service for our valves and ejectors. For each application, we define the valve's design, materials, inspection and test plan, and final preparation. “When Quality shall exceed the Standards…” Checks built into production Materials Positive material identification (PMI) on receipt. Surface and thickness Dye-penetrant inspection for surface defects after machining and welding; ultrasonic thickness checks on castings. Bellows Every bellows is pressure-tested and helium-tested. Pressure tests Hydrostatic body test and seat tightness test on every valve. Preparation Cleaning, drying, painting and tagging before shipment. Traceability Each valve's unique serial number links it to its manufacturer's certificate and EN 10204 3.1 material certificates. Tailor-made down to the paperwork: each valve ships with a certificate that names your specification and records its own tests. Our certificates and approvals Documents marked “on request” are sent after a short form, in their current revision. All Location Technical Quality management ISO 9001:2015 Quality management system, certified by LRQA. Free download AAR M-1003 Quality assurance for rail tank car valves (Association of American Railroads). On request Request → Nuclear quality assurance Quality assurance for nuclear projects to ASME NQA-1 and 10 CFR 50 Appendix B. On request Request → Euro Chlor GEST 17/492 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC bellows sealed globe valves, Euro Chlor approved (GEST 17/492) for liquid chlorine and dry chlorine gas, within defined sizes and classes. On request Request → SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) Globe valve series 1500, 2100, 2500 and 4025, 2200/2300 tank valves and BIMATIC actuators, certified by exida to IEC 61508. Free download Fugitive emissions (leaks to the air) Selected manual and on-off models type-tested to EN ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and TA Luft (German clean air regulation). On request Request → Hydrogen fluoride (HF) alkylation Licensor acceptance letters and declarations of conformity. On request Request → Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU Module H (full quality assurance): globe and lift check valves. European Union On request Request → ATEX (explosive atmospheres) Globe valves for potentially explosive atmospheres, compliant with directive 2014/34/EU; technical file lodged with a notified body. European Union On request Request → AAR tank car valves Approvals for models 921, 925 and 926. North America On request Request → Transport Canada TP14877 922/926 and 925/926 tank car valves compliant with standard TP14877. Canada On request Request → Canadian Registration Number (CRN) Registration of our valve range in Canada. Canada On request Request → China special equipment licence 2100 and 2500 manual and on-off valves. China On request Request → No document matches this filter. Need another document? Ask for a certificate, a declaration or a test report. Request a document What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. References Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. References Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia. Solutions Process / Piping Storage Transport Tailor-made Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "references.html", "t": "References: case studies, literature, FAQ | Descote V2", "h": "Proven in service", "d": "Field results, technical literature, certificates and answers on descote bellows sealed valves for chlorine, HF, HCN and nuclear duties.", "x": "Home ▸ References Proven in service Field results, technical documents and straight answers: the evidence behind descote valves for hazardous fluids. Explore our references Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia. → Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. → Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. → FAQ Short answers to the questions engineers and buyers ask us most often. → Every reference starts with a specification Each case began with one customer's specification. descote then built, tested and documented the valve. No two references are alike, but every valve behind them went through the same tests and traceability. Discuss your requirements Tell us about your application. We will point you to comparable references. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Overview Fluids & applications Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids. descote Company Our company, quality and certifications, worldwide presence and after-sales service. Solutions Process / Piping Storage Tailor-made Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related CN related Other critical applications Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "solution-fluid-transfer.html", "t": "Steam jet ejectors for fluid transfer | Descote V2", "h": "Fluid transfer: jets & ejectors", "d": "descote designs and manufactures steam jet ejectors to transfer radioactive and hazardous fluids with no moving parts, for nuclear and critical facilities.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Fluid transfer: jets & ejectors Steam jet ejectors that transfer hazardous and radioactive fluids without pumps or moving parts. Context and applications An ejector uses a motive fluid, usually steam, to draw in and move another fluid by the Venturi effect. With no moving parts, there is no shaft to seal and nothing to seize. descote designs and manufactures fluid transfer ejectors, a field covered by our ISO 9001 certification. Their main use is the nuclear industry: spent fuel reprocessing and research centres. Pre-engineered or tailor-made We adapt a field-proven ejector design to your fluid and conditions, or design a new one with you. Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Radioactive and toxic fluids No rotating part and no seal to wear: very little maintenance near the fluid. Predictable performance Designs characterised on our dedicated ejector test bench, including dilution rates. Proven designs A library of more than 2,000 ejector designs to start from. Typical solution families Steam jet transfer ejectors Motive steam transfers or draws radioactive and chemical solutions between vessels. Sampling and transfer modules Modules for sampling and moving fluids in nuclear facilities. Each ejector is sized for your fluid, flow and motive steam, drawing on data from our own test bench. Certifications & approvals ISO 9001:2015 Scope includes the design, manufacturing and sales of fluid transfer ejectors. Nuclear quality Nuclear quality assurance to ASME NQA-1 and 10 CFR 50 Appendix B. Proven in the field Ejector case studies are in preparation. Ask us for references in spent fuel reprocessing and research facilities. Share your application All case studies → Related literature Ask us for ejector technical data for your application. All literature → FAQ How does an ejector work? Motive steam accelerates through a nozzle and creates a low-pressure zone that draws in the fluid to be moved. The mixture then leaves through a diffuser. Is the transferred fluid diluted? Yes: the motive steam condenses into the fluid. We size each ejector to keep this dilution under control. All questions → Industries Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Fluids & applications All fluids & applications Other solutions Process / Piping Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, flow rate, lift and available motive steam. Send an inquiry What next? Industry Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations."}, {"u": "solution-instrumentation.html", "t": "Bellows sealed instrumentation valves, Model 2020 | Descote V2", "h": "Instrumentation valves", "d": "Model 2020 small-bore bellows sealed valves to isolate gauges, transmitters, flowmeters and sampling points on chlorine, HF, HCN and other hazardous lines.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Instrumentation Instrumentation valves Small-bore bellows sealed valves that isolate measuring and sampling points on hazardous fluid lines. Context and applications Every instrument connection carries the same fluid as the main line, and is one more potential leak point. Our Model 2020 brings bellows sealing down to small bore, from 1/8\" to 1/2\". It isolates pressure gauges, transmitters, level gauges and orifice flowmeters, and serves sample bottles, pilot units and laboratories. Pre-engineered or tailor-made We adapt the field-proven Model 2020 to your instrument line, or design a new valve with you. Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Stem tightness at small size Bellows sealing down to 1/8\", with secondary packing as back-up. Compact installations Forged body and a choice of end connections: butt-weld, socket-weld, threaded, compression tube fittings or flanges. Corrosive fluids Materials chosen for the process fluid, from stainless steel to nickel alloys such as Hastelloy® C-276. Manual or automated Manual, actuated on-off and control versions. Typical solution families Model 2020 Manual bellows sealed instrumentation globe valve with a forged body. Standard range 1/8\" to 1/2\", Class 150 to 1500, −80 °C to +400 °C. Handwheel operation Straight or angle body Model 2020A The 2020 fitted with a pneumatic actuator for remote on-off duty. A control version, 2020AC, is also available. Pneumatic actuator Solenoid valve and limit switches on request Even at half an inch, a descote valve is specified for your fluid, and every bellows is pressure-tested and helium-tested. Certifications & approvals Certificates on request. PED 2014/68/EU Pressure Equipment Directive: made under our quality system approved to module H; the category depends on size and fluid. CRN Model 2020 included in our Canadian Registration Number (CRN) scope. Proven in the field Instrumentation case studies are in preparation. Tell us about your application. Share your application All case studies → Related literature Instrumentation bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2020 Request All literature → FAQ Why a bellows sealed valve on an instrument line? A leak at a gauge or sampling point exposes operators as much as one on the main line. With a bellows, the packing is no longer the only barrier at the stem. Can the 2020 match our specification? Yes. Body material, end connections and pressure class are chosen for your line and fluid. Tell us your standard. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Petrochemicals Refineries, with HF alkylation units first. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Fluids & applications Also served Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Also served Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Also served CN related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Also served Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services. Other solutions Process / Piping Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, instrument type and connection standard. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed and gland packed globe valves, 3-way and check valves for process lines. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. References Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions."}, {"u": "solution-model-1000.html", "t": "UF6 valve Model 1000: 1-inch UF6 cylinder valve | Descote V2", "h": "UF6 valve – Model 1000", "d": "The descote Model 1000: 1-inch valve for 30B, 48X and 48Y UF6 cylinders, designed to ANSI N14.1 and supplied to the nuclear fuel cycle since 1978.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Transport ▸ UF6 valve Transport · Nuclear UF6 valve – Model 1000 The 1-inch valve that closes the uranium hexafluoride (UF6) cylinders travelling between conversion, enrichment and fuel fabrication plants around the world. One valve, the whole fuel cycle Each UF6 cylinder has a single valve: the only way in and out for the product. The cylinder is filled through it at the conversion plant, emptied and refilled at the enrichment plant, then emptied again at the fuel plant. In between, it travels by road, rail and sea. The valve must stay tight for the whole journey: handling, transport, and heating for liquid-phase filling and emptying. We have supplied 1-inch cylinder valves to the fuel cycle since 1978; in 1979, the US Department of Energy found them acceptable for its enrichment plants. What the valve must withstand UF6 chemistry UF6 reacts with moisture to form hydrogen fluoride (HF): materials and stem sealing are chosen for fluorinated service. Heat and cold Designed for −40 °C to +121 °C, from winter transport to hot filling and emptying. One interface for every cylinder A tinned 1\"-11½ NGT tapered thread that fits any compliant cylinder. Traceability Each valve is identified and supplied with its material certificates, as ANSI N14.1 requires. UF6 valve at a glance UF6 valve – Model 1000 1-inch cylinder valve designed to ANSI N14.1 (valve 51) and ISO 7195. 30B and 30C cylinders: enriched UF6 48X and 48Y cylinders: natural UF6 48G cylinders: depleted UF6 Every Model 1000 is assembled and tested in Feyzin, France, then traced by its own identification and material certificates: the same quality rules as our process valves. Certifications & approvals The standards the Model 1000 is designed to, and the approvals behind it. Certificates on request. ANSI N14.1 US standard for UF6 packaging: cylinders, valves and plugs. ISO 7195 International standard for UF6 transport packagings, derived from ANSI N14.1. US Department of Energy Our 1-inch cylinder valves found acceptable for its enrichment plants in 1979. Nuclear quality assurance Quality program to ASME NQA-1 and 10 CFR 50 Appendix B. Related literature 1-inch valve for UF6 cylinders Request Valves for the nuclear industry Request All literature → FAQ Can a valve removed from a cylinder be reused? No. ISO 7195 requires new valves and plugs: each Model 1000 is delivered new, identified and certified. Do you also supply cylinder plugs? Yes, plugs to ANSI N14.1. Tell us your cylinder types and quantities. All questions → Industries Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Fluids & applications Fluorine related Other solutions Transport Process / Piping Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Send us your cylinder types, quantities and destination country. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Transport Valves for rail tank cars and road tankers. Industry Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. References Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions."}, {"u": "solution-process-piping.html", "t": "Process & piping valves for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Process / Piping valves", "d": "Bellows sealed 2100B and 2500 globe valves, 1500B gland packed, 3-way and 8000 check valves for chlorine, HF alkylation, HCN and other Category M services.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Process / Piping Process / Piping valves Manual, on-off and control globe valves for the most hazardous process fluids. Context and applications All descote valves are designed for dangerous, corrosive, flammable and pyrophoric media. Many serve Category M fluids under ASME B31.3, where one small leak of chlorine, HF or HCN can cause serious harm. Pre-engineered or tailor-made We adapt a field-proven 2100B, 2500 or other process valve to your fluid and line, or design a new one with you. Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Stem leakage A welded metal bellows seals the stem; secondary packing backs it up. Deposits A hard knife-edge seat cuts through deposits. Operation Closing by pressing, not sliding: steady effort, even in an emergency. Typical solution families Also: 1500B gland packed valves, 3100/3500 3-way valves, BIMATIC actuators. ← → 2100B Protected bellows for liquefied gases, flashing and thermal shock. Standard range 1/2\" to 16\", −101 °C to +400 °C, up to Class 1500 (manual) or Class 600 (actuated). Manual 2100B On-off 2100BAT Control 2100BAC 2500 Flushed bellows, swept by the fluid, for fluids that polymerise or crystallise. Same standard range as the 2100B. Manual 2500 On-off 2500BAT Control 2500BAC 8000 Spring-loaded lift check valve against reverse flow. Lift check Materials are chosen for your fluid and pressure class, and incoming metal is checked by positive material identification (PMI). Certifications & approvals Certificates, approvals and declarations, on request. Euro Chlor 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC Euro Chlor approved (GEST 17/492). HF alkylation Accepted by licensor Honeywell UOP; manual and on-off valves declared compliant with MSS SP-160 and API RP 751. EN ISO 15848-1 Fugitive emissions, class AH-CO3; control valves excluded. SIL 3 capable Safety integrity level, IEC 61508: series 1500, 2100, 2500 and BIMATIC actuators. PED 2014/68/EU Pressure Equipment Directive, quality assurance module H. ATEX 2014/34/EU Compliant with the directive; technical file lodged with a notified body. Proven in the field Valve nest on top of a vessel, reached through the service grating. Europe · Liquid chlorine Chlorine feed line: 20 years without maintenance A 1-inch 2100B on a liquid chlorine feed line, maintenance-free in 2022. Process / Piping Chlorine related Chemicals Actuated bellows sealed globe valve on a process unit. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) HF alkylation in several refineries Isolation valves in HF alkylation units, praised for positive shut-off. Process / Piping Fluorine related Petrochemicals A row of manual globe valves with handwheels, ready for installation. Asia · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) 550+ valves for one HCN unit More than 550 manual and on-off 2500-series valves, 1\" to 6\", up to Class 1500, in a single HCN unit. Process / Piping CN related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Gland packed globe valve, Model 1500B Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Request 3-way valves, Models 3100 & 3500 Request Lift check valve, Model 8000 Request On-off actuated bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAT Request Control bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAC Request BIMATIC linear pneumatic actuator Request HF alkylation: process valves Request HF alkylation: small-size valves Request All literature → FAQ Can a globe valve replace a gate, plug or ball valve? It can, at the same face-to-face (installed length). Globe valves pass less flow than full-bore valves, so we check your flow coefficient (Cv) first. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Petrochemicals Refineries, with HF alkylation units first. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Fluids & applications Key fluid Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Key fluid Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Key fluid CN related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Also served Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services. Other solutions Instrumentation Storage Transport Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Share your fluid and conditions. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Fluid & application Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. References Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia."}, {"u": "solution-storage.html", "t": "Storage tank valves for liquefied toxic gases | Descote V2", "h": "Storage tank valves", "d": "2200 top and 2300 bottom tank valves: internal safety check valve, bellows sealed angle valve and spring-return actuator for chlorine and liquefied gases.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Storage Storage tank valves Top and bottom tank valves that keep liquefied toxic gases contained, and close remotely when it matters. Context and applications Most chemicals that are toxic by inhalation are stored as liquefied gases. On a storage tank, the valve is the last barrier between the product and the outside. Our 2200 and 2300 tank valves are designed for fluids such as chlorine, ammonia and other liquefied toxic gases. Pre-engineered or tailor-made We adapt a proven 2200/2300 design to your tank, or design a new one with you. Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Emergency isolation A spring-return actuator closes the valve, locally or by remote emergency command. Two barriers An internal safety check valve inside the tank, plus an external bellows sealed angle valve. Stem tightness Bellows sealing at the stem, with secondary packing as a second barrier. Typical solution families Top & bottom tank valves Complete tank valve assemblies with emergency control, in two versions. Standard range 1\" to 8\", Class 150 to 600, remotely operated. 2200 – tank top, bellows out of the flow 2300 – tank bottom, liquid outlet Dual-Tec™ seat option A hard metal seat, which withstands deposits and wear, combined with a soft seat for extra tightness. Your fluid, tank nozzle and shutdown logic set the design of each tank valve, built to the same quality plan as our process valves. Certifications & approvals Certificates on request. SIL 3 capable Models 2200 and 2300 certified by exida to IEC 61508, as components. EN ISO 15848-1 Models 2200 and 2300 type-tested to EN ISO 15848-1 (fugitive emissions). Proven in the field Actuated globe valves in descote yellow on an outdoor process line. Europe · Liquid and gaseous chlorine 400 valves for a new chlorine storage unit Manual, on-off, control and tank-bottom valves, 1\" to 10\", for storage, liquefaction and sampling. Process / Piping Storage Chlorine related Chemicals Top-mounted valves on a storage tank, painted descote yellow. North America · Anhydrous HF Anhydrous HF tank outlet Nickel-alloy bottom-outlet valves up to 8\": reliability study, helium testing, 18-metre manual extension. Storage Tailor-made Fluorine related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Storage tank valves, Models 2200 & 2300 Request All literature → FAQ Is a SIL 3 capable valve enough for a SIL 3 loop? Not on its own. The SIL applies to the whole safety loop – valve, actuator, solenoid valve and logic – and must be demonstrated for each application. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Petrochemicals Refineries, with HF alkylation units first. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Fluids & applications Key fluid Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Also served Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Also served CN related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Also served Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services. Other solutions Process / Piping Transport Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, tank nozzle and safety requirements. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Transport Valves for rail tank cars and road tankers. Fluid & application Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers."}, {"u": "solution-tailor-made.html", "t": "Tailor-made valve engineering for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "A valve defined for your fluid, process and standard", "d": "Valves defined for your fluid, process and standard: in-house engineering, bellows sealing, materials, testing and traceability, from Feyzin, France.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Tailor-made A valve defined for your fluid, process and standard When no existing design fits, our engineers define the valve with you, then we build and test it in Feyzin, France. Engineering approach Three inputs: your application, your specification and our own design rules, which can exceed the standards. Fluid Nature, state, moisture, toxicity, deposits. Conditions Pressure, temperature, flow direction, cycles. Standards Your specification, codes, approvals. Materials Body, bellows, stem, seats, bolting. Tightness Stem seal, seat, gasket. Tests & certificates A test plan and a traceable, documented valve. Built for one process Each valve shown here was built for one customer process: its medium, its pressure, its connections, its actuation. Phosgene / nitrogen Actuated bellows sealed globe valve UF6 Bellows sealed valve with star guided disc Hydrogen Actuated bellows sealed valve assembly BF3 High-pressure valve with diaphragm actuator Chlorine gas Bellows sealed angle valve for pressure tapping Knowledge of international and national standards We work to your industry's and country's codes, such as ASME B16.34 and B31.3, the EU Pressure Equipment Directive, Euro Chlor recommendations and API RP 751 for HF alkylation. Help choosing a specification Writing your own specification Help choosing a specification Tell us the fluid and conditions; we help you choose a specification, often a pre-engineered one. Solutions → Writing your own specification Starting from scratch? We bring a method, from the first questions to the finished valve. Tailor-made engineering → Project management & customer support Any deviation from your specification is listed for your approval; each valve then gets its own definition sheet, referenced on its certificate. Anti-corrosion protection Surface preparation & painting Paint system to suit the service, including chlorine-service and high-temperature systems. Automation & control valve sizing We size control valves and actuators in-house: flow coefficient (Cv), pressure drop, fail-safe position. Several valve series and our BIMATIC actuators are certified SIL 3 capable by exida. Tightness Stem seal to suit the fluid: closed bellows, open bellows or packing; each bellows is welded, backed by packing and helium-tested. Hard knife-edge seats cut through deposits, and listed models are type-tested to EN ISO 15848-1 for fugitive emissions. Fluid-based specification Liquefied, corrosive, moisture-sensitive or lethal: each fluid property changes the stem seal, materials, cleaning and tests. Chlorine valves are degreased and dried before shipping. Metallurgy & materials Carbon, low-temperature, stainless and duplex steels, Alloy 20 and nickel alloys, matched part by part to the fluid. Incoming metals are checked by positive material identification (PMI). Fluid mechanics Liquefied gases can flash, cavitate or cause thermal shock. We check flow and Cv for each service. NDT / NDE control Non-destructive testing (NDT/NDE): dye-penetrant inspection of every machined or welded part, ultrasonic checks on castings, radiography when your specification calls for it. Every valve then passes a hydrostatic shell test. Every design choice on this page traces back to your fluid, and every test result to your valve's serial number. Tailor-made in practice Top-mounted valves on a storage tank, painted descote yellow. North America · Anhydrous HF Anhydrous HF tank outlet Nickel-alloy bottom-outlet valves up to 8\": reliability study, helium testing, 18-metre manual extension. Storage Tailor-made Fluorine related Chemicals Large actuator on a valve assembly, with its control instrumentation. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) Bespoke actuator, HF alkylation safety system A 10-inch 2100HF valve replaced plug valves, with a fail-open actuator designed by descote. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Petrochemicals Pipe racks and valves of a process plant. Europe · Hydrogen Hydrogen at 420 bar A 1-inch Class 2500 gland packed valve for 420 bar, replacing a 2002 descote valve. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals All case studies → Customer support After sales Spare parts and approved repair shops. → Literature Datasheets and manuals. → Quality & certification Current certificates and approvals. → FAQ Can you help before our specification is frozen? Yes: we can help with sizing and material selection before your specification is frozen. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Petrochemicals Refineries, with HF alkylation units first. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Fluids & applications Also served Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Also served Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Also served CN related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Also served Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, ammonia, hot oil, molten salt and other severe services. Other solutions Process / Piping Instrumentation Transport Storage Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Discuss your requirements Share your fluid, conditions and specification: our engineers will answer. Send an inquiry What next? References Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia. descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. descote Company Our company, quality and certifications, worldwide presence and after-sales service."}, {"u": "solution-transport.html", "t": "Tank car valves for liquefied toxic gases | Descote V2", "h": "Transport valves", "d": "AAR-approved bellows sealed tank car valves with double closure for chlorine, anhydrous HF and HCl.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Transport Transport valves Valves that keep liquefied toxic gases contained on the move, by rail and road. Context and applications In transport, the valve is the barrier between the cargo and the public. It must withstand vibration and handling, limit the consequences of an accident and make loading and unloading safe. Our tank car valves were first approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR) in 1991. They serve chlorine, anhydrous hydrogen fluoride and anhydrous hydrogen chloride. Pre-engineered or tailor-made We adapt a field-proven transport valve to your cargo and tank, or design a new one with you. Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Containment after an accident Double closure: the tank stays closed even if the external valve is torn off. No operator on the tank Remote operation from the loading station, and automatic closure if the car moves during transfer. Stem tightness Bellows sealing, backed by an emergency stuffing box. Maintenance The main valve can be replaced without degassing the tank. Typical solution families ← → Road & rail transport valves Angle valves for tank cars and road tankers. 921 manual valve 922/926 manual valve + internal check valve 925/926 pneumatic valve + internal check valve Valves for ISO containers ISO tank containers for liquefied hazardous gases are part of our transport scope. Ask us about valve options for your container and fluid. UF6 valve – Model 1000 1-inch valve for UF6 cylinders. The 925/926 exists in separate approved versions for chlorine, anhydrous HF and anhydrous HCl: each valve is matched to its cargo, then traced by a unique serial number and certified material test reports. Certifications & approvals Approvals, and the standards our designs follow. Certificates on request. AAR Models 921 and 925/926 approved; our Feyzin plant audited to AAR M-1003 quality requirements. Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 168 Double-closure designs follow this guideline for bulk chlorine transport. Transport Canada 922/926 and 925/926 compliant with standard TP14877. Proven in the field Valves inside the protective housing of a rail tank car, seen from above. North America · Liquid chlorine Chlorine tank cars across North America Over 1,000 double-closure 922/926 valves: bellows sealed angle valve plus internal check valve. Transport Chlorine related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Trailer & rail transportation valves Request All literature → FAQ What does double closure mean on a tank car? Two independent barriers: an internal spring-loaded ball check valve under the cover plate, and an external bellows sealed angle valve. How are valves prepared for chlorine service? They are degreased, dried for three hours and sealed before shipping. All questions → Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, and for research facilities. Fluids & applications Key fluid Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Also served Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Other solutions Process / Piping Storage Tailor-made UF6 valve Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, container type and applicable regulations. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Storage Top and bottom tank valves with an internal safety check valve and remote closure. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. descote After sales Spare parts and approved repair shops."}, {"u": "solutions.html", "t": "Valve solutions for hazardous applications | Descote V2", "h": "Valve solutions for hazardous applications", "d": "Bellows sealed valves and ejectors for chlorine, HF, HCN and other hazardous fluids: pre-engineered bases adapted to your fluid, or tailor-made engineering from scratch.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions Valve solutions for hazardous applications Every descote valve starts from your fluid, your process and your standards. Choose a proven base or start from a blank page: either way, it is engineered for you. Five product families Process / Piping Bellows sealed and gland packed globe valves, 3-way and check valves for process lines. → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for gauges, transmitters and sampling points. → Storage Top and bottom tank valves with an internal safety check valve and remote closure. → Transport Valves for rail tank cars and road tankers. → Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Ejectors driven by steam move radioactive and hazardous fluids, with no pump and no moving parts. → Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. → Pre-engineered or tailor-made? Pre-engineered does not mean off the shelf: we start from a field-proven design and help you define the right specification for your application. Tailor-made engineering goes further: our engineers help you build your own specification from scratch, with a proven method. In both cases, the same metallurgy expertise, testing and full traceability apply. Start from your fluid or your sector Fluids & applications → Industries → Every valve starts from your fluid and your process. Discuss your requirements Tell us about your fluid, operating conditions and standards. Our engineers will help you define the right valve. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Overview Fluids & applications Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids. Overview Industries Chemicals, agrochemicals, petrochemicals and nuclear."}, {"u": "terms.html", "t": "Terms and Conditions | Descote V2", "h": "Terms and Conditions", "d": "Terms and conditions for using the descote website: access, intellectual property, technical information, liability and applicable law.", "x": "Home ▸ Terms and Conditions Terms and Conditions The terms that apply when you use the descote website. Legal text to be supplied by descote. The outline below lists the sections the final terms will cover. Terms of website use 1. Publisher and scope Identifies DESCOTE S.A.S. as publisher of the website and states who these terms apply to. Company details are given in our Legal notices. Legal notices → 2. Access to the website Availability of the website, maintenance, and our right to change, suspend or close it. 3. Intellectual property Protection of texts, photographs, drawings, videos, logos and descote trademarks, and the conditions for any reuse. 4. Technical information States that product information on this website is general and not contractual: each descote valve is defined for a specific application, and only descote's written proposal is binding. 5. Documents and literature Conditions for accessing and using brochures, manuals and other documents, including those available on request. Literature → 6. Inquiries and quotations States that sending a form does not place an order, and which terms govern descote offers and sales. 7. Liability Limits of liability for the use of the website and its content. 8. Links Links from this website to third-party websites, and links to this website. 9. Personal data and cookies How we handle personal data and cookies: see our Privacy Policy and Cookie Policy. Privacy Policy → 10. Changes to these terms How and when these terms may be updated, and the date of the current version. 11. Applicable law and jurisdiction Governing law and competent courts. 12. Contact DESCOTE S.A.S., 9 Avenue Jean Jaurès, 69320 Feyzin – France. info@descote.com Information on this site is general by design: every descote valve is defined, validated and tested for one specific application, and only a written descote proposal applies to it. A question about these terms? Please contact us through our inquiry form. Contact us What next? Legal information Legal notices Legal information Privacy Policy Legal information Cookie Policy Which cookies this website uses, why, and how to change your choice."}, {"u": "globally.html", "t": "Our worldwide presence | Descote V2", "h": "Globally", "d": "Our worldwide presence ensures local support, faster delivery, and tailored solutions wherever you are.", "x": "Home ▸ Globally Globally 62 countries served 9 repair shops 1 headquarters — Feyzin, France Need to contact us ? Need to get info ? All contacts Global presence Main Repair shops Countries served Repair shops Headquarters — Feyzin, France Global presence — 62 countries Argentina Australia Austria Bangladesh Belgium Brazil Bulgaria Canada Chile China Colombia Croatia Czech Republic Denmark Ecuador Egypt Finland France Germany Greece Hungary India Indonesia Ireland Israel Italy Japan Jordan Kuwait Malaysia Mexico Morocco Netherlands New Caledonia New Zealand Norway Pakistan Peru Poland Portugal Qatar Romania Saudi Arabia Serbia Singapore Slovak Republic Slovenia South Africa South Korea Spain Sweden Switzerland Taiwan Thailand Tunisia Turkey United Arab Emirates United Kingdom USA Uzbekistan Venezuela Vietnam Repair shops Belgium Brazil China France Mexico Netherlands Taiwan United Kingdom USA Plus two local offices: Shanghai (China) and Baton Rouge (USA). Main — headquarters descote International 9 Avenue Jean Jaurès 69320 FEYZIN – FRANCE +33 4 72 89 25 00 Fax +33 4 72 89 25 25 info@descote.com Need a quotation or after-sales support? Our team answers every request from Feyzin. Inquiry Our subsidiaries descote Inc. – Baton Rouge, USA 11529 Sun Belt Court, Baton Rouge, Louisiana 70809 info.usa@descote.com Local stock of valves and actuators. descote Valve (Shanghai) Co., Ltd. – China 1126 Beisong Road, Minhang District, Shanghai 201111 Stock, customisation and after-sales for Asia-Pacific. Local contacts, one factory: wherever your plant is, your valve is designed and manufactured in Feyzin. Need a repair near your plant? Select “Repair shops” on the map above to find one near your plant, or see how we train repairers and supply genuine parts. After sales What next? descote Company Our company, quality and certifications, worldwide presence and after-sales service. descote Quality & Certification Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Solutions All solutions Fluids & applications All fluids & applications"}, {"u": "inquiry.html", "t": "Inquiry | Descote V2", "h": "Contact", "d": "Get in touch with our experts for tailored guidance, pricing requests, or product insights—our know-how is at your service.", "x": "Home ▸ Inquiry Contact Request for quotation, after-sales service, maintenance or application study: tell us what you need. Name Company Email Industry (optional) — Chemicals Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Other Your message I agree that my details are used to answer my request, as described in the Privacy Policy . Send my message Mock-up: nothing is sent. Thank you — your message has been noted. The descote team will get back to you shortly. descote 9 Avenue Jean Jaurès 69320 Feyzin – France +33 4 72 89 25 00 info@descote.com Worldwide Partners and repair shops close to your plants. Our network Every descote valve is defined for your fluid, your process and your standard. A few lines are enough to start: our engineers will ask for the rest. What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. descote After sales Spare parts and approved repair shops. descote Globally Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. Solutions Tailor-made All solutions"}, {"u": "join-us.html", "t": "Join us | Descote V2", "h": "Join us", "d": "Join descote in Feyzin, near Lyon, France: valve solutions for hazardous fluids. See our job openings or send an unsolicited application.", "x": "Home ▸ Join us Join us Chart a Course for Excellence - Join Us! Chart a Course for Excellence - Join Us! For over 50 years, our company, based in Feyzin (Lyon, France), has been designing and manufacturing valve solutions for hazardous fluids. On the demanding path of industrial progress, this family-owned business has stayed true to its founder’s original vision—with a lasting ambition: to protect people, drive sustainable innovation, and tackle the industry’s most critical challenges. Joining descote means stepping aboard for the long haul. Every team member is part of the crew—engaged in a shared mission where everyone plays a vital role. We pursue excellence and continuous improvement as our true north, helping us move forward together, no matter how rough the waters. Our playground? The entire world. Our edge? Advanced technology, powered by exceptional human chemistry. Looking for a company where your expertise is valued, innovation never stops, and every project has a purpose? Come aboard! descote in short Family-owned since 1974 · Feyzin (Lyon, France) Valve solutions for hazardous fluids Chemicals · Agrochemicals · Petrochemicals · Nuclear Working at descote means building valves that are each defined for one customer's fluid, then machined, assembled and tested on our own benches in Feyzin. Career Opportunities CDI Technicien tourneur vertical traditionnel (H/F) See the offer None of the offers suit you? Use the form below to send us a speculative application and explain why you would like to join us. You have talent, we have challenges First name Last name Email Phone (optional) Type of request Unsolicited application Apply to an offer Offer (optional) — Technicien tourneur vertical traditionnel (H/F) Tell us about you Add my resume (optional) Add my cover letter (optional) I agree that my details are used to process my application, as described in the Privacy Policy . Send my application Mock-up: nothing is sent. Thank you — your application has been noted. We will come back to you soon. What next? descote Company Our company, quality and certifications, worldwide presence and after-sales service. descote Globally Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. Solution Tailor-made engineering When no existing design fits: a valve specified from scratch with our engineers. Solutions Tailor-made Fluids & applications All fluids & applications"}, {"u": "legal-notices.html", "t": "Legal notices | Descote V2", "h": "Legal notices", "d": "Legal notices for the descote website: publisher, hosting, terms of website use, intellectual property and personal data.", "x": "Home ▸ Legal notices Legal notices Site provided by: DESCOTE 9 Av. Jean Jaurès Rue des Frères Lumière 69320 Feyzin – France Tél. : +33 (0)4 72 89 25 00 email : info@descote.com SIRET : 302 046 586 00046 RCS : 302 046 586 R.C.S. Lyon SAS with capital of € 1 659 300,00 Publishing Director: Vincent RICHER Contact : info@descote.com Web design and site development: Les Imageurs Hosting: Evoliatis 26 rue Bergson, 42000 Saint-Étienne Tél : 04 28 04 05 25 Terms of website use This page details the terms of use on which you may make use of any of the websites owned and managed by Us (\"our websites\"), whether as a guest or a registered user. Please read these terms of use carefully before you start to use a website. By using one of our websites, you indicate that you accept these terms of use and that you agree to abide by them. If you do not agree to these terms of use, please refrain from using any of our websites. Intellectual property The contents of this web site, text, images, sounds, animations, etc. as well as the graphic design and source code are protected by French and international law regarding the intellectual and industrial property rights of Steel Projects SAS. As such, their reproduction, distribution, public communication and transformation, totally or partially, is prohibited without the express authorization of Steel Projects SAS and constitutes an infringement sanctioned by articles L. 335-2 et seq. of the intellectual property code. Privacy Policy Steel Projects SAS informs that the personal data facilitated of voluntary form in this web site will be object of treatmen automated and incorporated to the corresponding files. The data incorporated to our files are absolutely confidential and will be dealed with the highest confidentiality and fulfilling all the requirements with Organic Law 13 of December 15/1999 on the Protection of Personal Data. The user will be able to use his right of access, rectification, cancellation and opposition of this data. Their personal data will not be yielded nor transferred to third. Cookies We may collect information about your computer, including where available your IP address, operating system and browser type, for system administration and to report aggregate information. This is statistical data about our users' browsing actions and patterns, and does not identify any individual. This information may be stored in a cookie on your computer or in a log file on our web server. A cookie is a small text file stored on the hard disk of your computer. Its contents are not transferred to or made available to any 3rd parties. We may also record statistics about which pages of our website you look at and include this information with any online form submissions you make. Our website uses cookies to identify registered users. Certain pages on our website are reserved for users who have completed and submitted a registration form. The cookie file does not contain your registration information but is used to verify your username and password when accessing certain pages and information on our website. You may refuse to accept cookies by adjusting the settings on your browser, however if you choose to do so you will not be able to access certain parts of our site. Our site changes regularly We aim to update our site regularly, and may change the content at any time. If the need arises, we may suspend access to our site, or close it indefinitely. Any of the material on our site may be out of date at any given time, and we are under no obligation to update such material. Les informations contenues dans ce site sont non contractuelles et sujettes à modification sans préavis. Web content and links Steel Projects SAS will not be held liable for the incorrect use which may occur to the contents on our web site, being the sole responsibility of the person that accesses or uses them. Nor do we assume any responsibility for the information contained on the web sites related to third parties which can be accessed by links or browsers from this web site. Events outside our control The service is normally accessible 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. We will not be liable or responsible for any failure to perform, or delay in performance of, any of our obligations under a Contract that is caused by events outside our reasonable control (\"Force Majeure Event\"). Our right to vary these terms and conditions We have the right to revise and amend any of our terms and conditions or policies from time to time. Behind this website, a manufacturer: in Feyzin, descote defines each valve for its customer's fluid, process and standard, then builds and tests it. What next? Legal information Privacy Policy Legal information Cookie Policy Which cookies this website uses, why, and how to change your choice. Legal information Terms and Conditions The terms that apply when you use the descote website."}, {"u": "privacy-policy.html", "t": "Privacy Policy | Descote V2", "h": "Privacy Policy", "d": "How descote uses the personal data sent through its contact forms, which browsing data it keeps, and how to correct or delete your data.", "x": "Home ▸ Privacy Policy Privacy Policy Personal information When you submit the contact form, DESCOTE may store: your surname, first name and e-mail address. Your consent is confirmed as soon as you submit the contact form. The form can only be validated if the box certifying your consent has been ticked. How do we use your data? DESCOTE uses your data to manage its customer/prospect relations. Their purpose is to facilitate the follow-up of assignments that have been entrusted to the centre and/or to send news and information that may be of interest to you. Browsing information (cookies) DESCOTE does not collect any personal data when you browse this site. Your IP address is completely anonymised and it is impossible to geolocate you. The only data we store is : the source of your visit (search engines, social networks, links, etc.) your use of the site (pages viewed, reading time, etc.) the hardware used (support, browser, screen size) We therefore consider that the cookies added to your computer are necessary for the site to function properly and for the site to be user-friendly during your visit. However, you can block the collection of cookies during your browsing. To do this, you need to change your browser settings. The settings for cookies are generally found in the \"Options\" or \"Preferences\" menu of your Internet browser. The following links will help you understand how to adjust these settings: Cookies used Our website uses cookies to ensure that certain parts of the website function correctly and that your preferences as a user are taken into account. These so-called \"functional\" cookies do not require your consent. Name of service provider Cookie name Shelf life Purpose DESCOTE _pk_id.nnnn 13 months Stores your unique visit identifier DESCOTE _pk_ref.nnnn 6 months Records the means by which you arrived on the site DESCOTE _pk_ses.nnnn 30 mins Allows temporary storage of your visit data DESCOTE hasConsent 7 months No longer displays the Cookies popup How do we use your data? DESCOTE uses your data to manage its customer/prospect relations. Their purpose is to facilitate the follow-up of assignments that have been entrusted to the centre and/or to send news and information that may be of interest to you. Your consent is given when you browse this site. Browsing information is used to provide you with an optimal browsing experience and to ensure the smooth operation of the services. Who has access to your data? DESCOTE staff may have internal access to your data. Subject to the user's contraindication, we may also be asked to pass on your data to our partners in order to carry out the tasks you have entrusted to us. These people may contact you directly using the contact details you have given us. They are not authorised to use your personal information other than for these purposes, and are required to keep it confidential. Where is your data stored? We use various security procedures to ensure the best possible protection for your personal data. Your personal data is stored in a secure, controlled computer area that is protected against unauthorised access. We also use the SSL encryption protocol on all pages of the https://www.descote.com website. The aim of these measures is to minimise the risk of unauthorised access to your data. However, there is no such thing as zero risk. How long will your data be kept? In order to respond as effectively as possible to the tasks entrusted to us, DESCOTE retains your data until the purpose for which it was collected has been fulfilled. Thereafter, your data will be deleted from our database. Navigation data (cookies) will be kept for 13 months, in accordance with regulations. Personal data will be kept for a maximum of 24 months, the retention period used to manage canvassing or commercial relations. You have the right to rectification, the right to be forgotten and the right to have your personal data deleted at any time. How can you access your data? If you identify an error in your personal data, or if you consider them to be incomplete or inappropriate, you may ask us to correct, complete or delete them. You can contact us by e-mail(info@descote.com), by telephone on +334 72 89 25 00, or by post at DESCOTE, 9 Av. Jean Jaurès Rue des Frères Lumière, 69320 Feyzin – France to ask us to take the necessary action. How can I unsubscribe from our communications? You can unsubscribe from our e-mails at any time by clicking on the \"Change your preferences\" or \"Unsubscribe from all lists\" links. You will find these links at the bottom of all our marketing and sales e-mails. You can also contact us by e-mail(info@descote.com), by telephone on +334 72 89 25 00 or by post at DESCOTE, 9 Av. Jean Jaurès Rue des Frères Lumière, 69320 Feyzin – France. We will continue to send you e-mails unless you change your mind or notify us otherwise. Every descote valve starts from what you tell us: your fluid, your process and your standard. What next? Legal information Cookie Policy Which cookies this website uses, why, and how to change your choice. Legal information Terms and Conditions The terms that apply when you use the descote website. Legal information Legal notices"}, {"u": "index-egalite.html", "t": "Index égalité professionnelle femmes hommes | Descote V2", "h": "Index égalité professionnelle", "d": "Index de l'égalité professionnelle femmes-hommes de descote : résultats 2026 (données 2025) des indicateurs calculables.", "x": "Home ▸ Index égalité professionnelle Index égalité professionnelle Index égalité professionnelle femmes hommes La valeur de notre index 2026 basé sur les données 2025 n’a pas pu être calculé en raison de la nature de nos effectifs. Seuls deux indicateurs ont donné des résultats : Indicateur relatif à l’écart de rémunération : incalculable Indicateur relatif à l’écart de taux d’augmentation individuelles : 25 points / 35 Indicateur relatif au pourcentage de salariées ayant bénéficié d’une augmentation dans l’année suivant leur congé maternité : incalculable Indicateur relatif à la représentation parmi les plus hautes rémunérations : 5 point / 10 À Feyzin, nos équipes conçoivent, fabriquent et testent chaque vanne pour le fluide, le procédé et la norme de nos clients. What next? descote Careers Chart a Course for Excellence - Join Us! descote Company Our company, quality and certifications, worldwide presence and after-sales service. Legal information Legal notices"}];
